In article <1991Mar4.215058.4660@news.cs.brandeis.edu> cos@chaos.cs.brandeis.edu (Ofer Inbar) writes:

A spoiler, which should be <CTRL-L>'d:

>2) As long as you haven't speeded your pet faster than you, you don't
>have to let him eat the floating eyes.  Just stand right next to the
>eye (it won't move) and *don't hurt it*.  Let your pet do the
>fighting.  Eventually, he will kill it.  As sson as he does so, move
>onto the corpse.  He can't both kill the eye and move onto it at the
>same time.

Actually, pets are fast to start with.  Your pet *can* both kill
the eye and move onto it between two of your moves.  This trick
seems to work *most* of the time, though.  I use it, when I don't
have a blindfold or a wand of invisibility (i.e., most of the time
in the early part of a game).

The phrase, "speeded your pet faster than you" is a bit misleading
as well.  If you and a monster are both double speed, you hit twice
and then the monster hits twice.  Even if you are faster than your
pet, it can still do several things between your moves.

